+# Complete composition collection
+
+2026-10-28. Kriv authorized continuing the remaining designs using Astra. This
+completes the structural rebuild of the existing 26-design library for local
+review. All 26 remain in cross-industry rotation. No public release is implied.
+
+## What changed
+
+The original Linen/Canvas, Ledger/Index and Torque/Stage remain intact. The other
+23 now own separate homepage structures, rather than selecting the same hero and
+section sequence with different colors. Examples include Table's facing book
+leaves, Gloss's portrait and oversized overlapping typography, Workshop's ruled
+photographic plate, Mane's right navigation rail, Shore's rising caption card and
+Pressure's perforated message ticket. Existing fonts, palettes and template IDs
+remain, with updated fingerprints describing their new structural identities.
+
+Each composition owns its hero, navigation treatment, content order and offering
+arrangement. Shared content components render supplied facts and safe links.
+Native service disclosures support touch, keyboard and JavaScript-disabled use;
+story and question disclosures reveal supplied information only. Mobile layouts
+recompose vertically. Motion is limited to short control feedback and disclosure
+entrances, with a reduced-motion alternative. No scroll handler or animation/UI
+dependency was added. Next.js, React, CSS Modules and the standalone Desk remain.
+
+Every default composition works across industries: contentNiche supplies the
+business's terminology separately from the design ID. Existing records are not
+bulk migrated. Explicit saved design.sections overrides retain their established
+renderer. The three original comparison samples retain the same fictional
+business and credited architectural image; the other 23 fictional records and
+their reviewed, credited photographs are unchanged. A single photo is used as a
+scene rather than repeated to manufacture a gallery. A real multi-photo record
+can still use the existing accessible GalleryViewer.
+
+The source gallery now has an actual screenshot on every design card. Lead Desk's
+existing picker reads all 26 composition labels and signatures automatically.
+The four new presentation files participate in visual-version hashing: changing
+the code invalidates stale visual approval while keeping decision history.
+Refresh verification captures before visually reviewing an affected concept.
+Publication and outreach still require their separate founder actions.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Preview lint, typecheck, 357 tests across 12 files, production build and all
+  16 smoke checks pass. Full/minimal data, all 26 safeguards, cross-industry
+  labels, saved overrides and version-bound approval history are covered.
+- Source lint and webpack production build pass. The documented local dependency
+  junction workaround remains; no framework/configuration migration was needed.
+- 156 browser cases: 26 designs at 1440, 768 and 390 pixels under both motion
+  preferences, including real touch emulation on phones, native disclosures,
+  keyboard controls, image loading, inert actions, emphasis visibility, number
+  wrapping and horizontal overflow. All 26 also pass native fallbacks at 320
+  pixels with JavaScript disabled. There are zero browser console/page errors.
+- Actual About navigation passes for every design at desktop and phone widths
+  (52 journeys). Source checks pass 287 known pages, four anonymous not-found
+  views, and 78 About/Contact/service-detail captures across all 13 content niches.
+  The source's existing streamed-404 HTTP status limitation is unchanged; the
+  preview application still passes actual unknown/draft 404 checks.
+- Gallery checks pass at 1440/768/390 with all 26 actual thumbnails loaded and
+  keyboard navigation into a sample. Fourteen desktop/phone hero and service
+  review sheets were visually inspected. Review prompted fixes to inverted
+  accent-word contrast, a narrow phone headline, wrapped service numbers and
+  repeated service introductions; affected full-size captures were rechecked.
+- The isolated synthetic Lead Desk journey passes with zero actual network
+  requests or private data access: search, queues, visual decisions, failed-save
+  protection, reload persistence, publication confirmation/cancel, verification
+  retry, manual sent status and follow-up. Four new tests ensure each new
+  presentation file invalidates stale approval without deleting decisions.
+
+These are local Chromium/synthetic checks, not a physical-phone, assistive-
+technology or production Core Web Vitals audit. Public configured fonts were
+loaded with authorized network access. The main matrix uses previously reviewed
+local image fixtures; source navigation also loaded the public image URLs.
+New home layouts are server-rendered; the only optional interactive client
+boundary is the already-existing gallery viewer. No performance score is claimed.
+
+## Preservation and synchronization
+
+No real lead contents, private database contents, email drafts or secrets were
+inspected. The existing chucks-ducts.json edit is untouched and excluded. No new
+service, price, credential, testimonial or photograph was added to a real record.
+No finder qualification, paid service, publishing workflow, noindex rule,
+concept notice or inert business action was removed or bypassed.
+
+Root baseline: e1c9694. Source baseline: 688cdbb. Both use the approved
+claude/amazing-edison-juyem3 branch. The new Collection files, template registry,
+definitions and renderer are mirrored into the local source checkout; only the
+expected address region/province adaptation differs. Gallery app changes,
+thumbnails and fictional records remain source-only. See SYNC.md.
+
+Delivery was completed by Claude Code on 2026-10-28 after a Codex handoff. This
+collection is saved as one local source commit on the approved branch, based on
+688cdbb; the preview repository records its SHA and a binary zero-context export
+at docs/reports/site-arsenal-2026-10-28-complete-collection.patch. Review and
+apply with git apply --unidiff-zero against that base. Earlier checkpoints and
+exports remain. No push, merge or deployment was performed.
+
+## Review locally
+
+Lead Desk: http://localhost:4321. Gallery: http://localhost:3101.
+Kriv reviews the designs and decides which need further refinement. Approval of
+these local changes does not authorize publishing a real lead or sending email.
+
